### Changes

The [yin.repl-test gate](/tmp/datomworld-gate-80e2ad00/test/yin/repl_test.cljc:191) keeps the Python switch and the refusal shape on every host. It adds a generic `installed:` check. Only the PHP switch, language pin, and compile preview run off Dart. On Dart it asserts the PHP refusal, the installed list, and that the session stays on `:yang/clojure`.

The [yin.repl.main-test gate](/tmp/datomworld-gate-80e2ad00/test/yin/repl/main_test.cljc:340) keeps the refusal shape generic on every host. The exact PHP-including installed list runs only off Dart, mirroring the [host-gate pattern](https://github.com/sonwh98/datomworld/commit/9032649e0478a6b23af2f8bdbcf3426eddb9a32f). On Dart it asserts the PHP refusal and that the PHP source does not evaluate to `3`. The Clojure tail still runs on every host. No assertions were deleted.

